"""pli-reglages-inventaire : inventory of all PLI settings, replayable.

Reads the code (without loading a model or importing MLX):
  - the options of `pli serve` (parser in src/pli/cli_args.py);
  - the PLI_* variables (and the two production MLX_*) read in src/ (AST analysis: os.environ.get, getenv,
    os.environ[...], "X" in os.environ, and the small reading functions in the code);
  - the old names (src/pli/additions/env_names.py);
  - the keys of the JSON generation files (repository examples, reading location in src/pli/gen).

Writes:
  - src/pli/config/table.json: the settings table read by `pli config:*` (portable, nothing from the machine);
  - docs/reglages.md, between the markers « debut inventaire » and « fin inventaire » (the rest of the file is kept);
    the « production » columns come from the production files if they exist on the machine (read-only).

Usage :
  tools/pli-reglages-inventaire                 writes the two files
  tools/pli-reglages-inventaire --verifier      exit code 1 if table.json is no longer up to date (nothing is written)
  tools/pli-reglages-inventaire --prod-env A.env --prod-env B.env --prod-yaml config.yaml --prod-json gen/*.json
"""

